In a previous article, esot@troi.cc.rochester.edu (Eric Sotnak) says:

>  I have a blessed magic marker (58) and 6 blank scrolls (ala w. of
>cancellation).  So, I tried writing a scroll of genocide by writing
>"genocide".  The result was a message to the effect that "you don't know how
>to write that."  So what do I need to do?  I also have the option of
>blessing the blank scrolls.  Would that help?  What other scrolls might be
>good to create?
>

	Unfortunately (for you), you cannot write a scroll of any 
particular type until you have identified that type of scroll. When 
you find a scroll of genocide and identify it (by reading it or by 
using a scroll/spellbook of identify on it) you will be able to write
scrolls of genocide. Beware, though, that high-level scrolls like
genocide, while undeniably useful, tend to use up your magic marker
very quickly. Writing a worthless scroll like "light" may only
reduce your magic marker charges by a few points, but "genocide"
is likely to use 20 points or so.
	Don't bother blessing your scrolls; a blessed magic marker
will write blessed scrolls, if the blank paper is uncursed or blessed.
The paper/magic marker relation is:

				If your magic
				marker is:

				cursed		uncursed	blessed
	And your blank	+--------------------------------------------------+
	paper is:	|	Then the scroll you write will be:	   |
			|						   |
	cursed		|	cursed		cursed		uncursed   |
			|						   |
	uncursed	|	cursed		uncursed	blessed	   |
			|						   |
	blessed		|	uncursed	blessed		blessed    |
			+--------------------------------------------------+

	Which is really pretty simple, but if I just _explained_ it,
I wouldn't have this impressive chart to post... :)
	Note that since some scrolls are especially useful when _cursed_,
it may not always be the greatest idea to bless your magic marker. Blessing
your magic marker can save a lot of holy water if you want to write blessed
scrolls, but you _cannot_ write a cursed scroll with a blessed magic marker.

